5. EXCEPTIONS: FAMILIES WHOSE LICENSE DIFFERS FROM BSD-3-CLAUSE

These are not covered by section 1. Each folder holds its own license text.

- ports/doom/: GPL-2.0 (the Doom port; ports/doom/LICENSE).
- ports/bitnetmcu/ and third-party/bitnetmcu/: GPL-3.0.
- ports/openocd-cc23xx/: GPL-2.0-or-later (the OpenOCD flash driver).
- am62l-evm/linux/cpu1_start/ and am62l-evm/rpmsg/: the Linux kernel module sources are GPL-2.0.
- ports/esphome-ti/: GPLv3 for the ESPHome runtime the shim sources compile into; see
  ports/esphome-ti/LICENSE.
- third-party/arduino/ArduinoCore-API: LGPL-2.1.
- Four files under the TI Limited License, for use only with TI devices, not BSD-3-Clause:
  cc35x1/matter/thermostat/csi/ti/feature_extract.c and feature_extract.h,
  cc2340r5/zigbee/onoff_light/dmm/rcl_stub_dmm.c and cc2340r5/zigbee-alarm/dmm/rcl_stub_dmm.c
  (LICENSE-TI-LIMITED.txt in each folder).
- ports/microwakeword/models/hey_sparky.tflite and hey_sparky.json: non-commercial, personal use
  only (ports/microwakeword/models/LICENSE). A firmware image that embeds the model carries
  the same limit.

Hardware safety: this repository contains programs that erase and rewrite a microcontroller's
flash memory and scripts that drive debug probes. They are provided as is, for development
boards, with no warranty; read each folder's README before running anything on a board.
